ounds to 2.66 and 2.675 rounds to 2.68, which is what the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), against `main`. Alex wasn't added as a reviewer when the PR was created, so I requested the review separately and he's on it now.\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the security advisory lookup. That's probably fine because it seems to be an internal finance reference, not a security advisory. I took the ROUND_HALF_EVEN requirement from the docstring and the test, which agree.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HgetgeaPt9FdjVnhrGvD7J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013UuWRzuXWW744kEapw4wkT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016AKUFnRemk58xdBvRqK1uN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BKdUMRy3uWns7qC6DbAbPf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011aXz1s2qM6ktHFDoKjGFEP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_m